    "body": "Prepares v0.1.0 by closing the biggest documentation gaps. Five files, no source code changes.\n\n## New files\n\n**docs/current-state.md** -- what renders, what does not, and why. Includes:\n- A demo screenshot showing the pipeline working end-to-end\n- A \"what renders correctly\" table with per-feature PR references\n- A \"what does not render\" table linking each gap to a planned ADR\n- A per-property breakdown of example.com's stylesheet explaining why it renders as a text dump in HoneyBee but not in Firefox\n\n**docs/decisions/README.md** -- index of all 12 ADRs with one-line summaries and a recommended reading order.\n\n**docs/demo-screenshot.png** -- screenshot of docs/demo.html rendering in HoneyBee v0.1.0.\n\n## Edits\n\n**README.md** -- new \"What Works Today\" section with a feature matrix and the demo screenshot.\n\n**CONTRIBUTING.md** -- three updates:\n- Fixed stale build commands to match CI\n- Replaced \"tests not set up yet\" with actual state (154 cases, 644 assertions)\n- New \"Known Gotchas\" section covering five failure modes we actually hit during ADR-008 through ADR-013\n\n## Why now\n\nWe are about to tag v0.1.0. A stranger landing on the repo will click README first and currently see no answer to \"what works.\" They will click docs/decisions/ and see 12 files with no index. All of that is fixable in one docs PR, and doing it before the tag means the release points at documentation that answers the question honestly -- including where the pipeline falls short.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Build: no-op (docs only)\n- Tests: 154 cases, 644 assertions, all pass (unchanged)\n- Screenshot: captured live from ./build/bin/honeybee loading docs/demo.html via a local HTTP server\n\n## Known policy drift (not addressed here)\n\nADR-002 specifies Arabic for README and docs. In practice, README is English and ADRs 007-013 are English. This PR matches the actual state rather than rewriting everything in Arabic. A future ADR should reconcile the policy.\n",
